    "narrative": "For today's matchup, our highest ceiling resides with **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 73.46 makes him our premier start. Benefitting from a favorable 4.59 xERA matchup against Wesneski and a prime #2 lineup spot, **Lawrence Butler** leverages a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost and positive park factors to anchor our production. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.32) and **Cal Raleigh** (65.23) follow closely; while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** carries a slight historical BvP drag, his elite talent profile and high-leverage #2 spot against Wacha remain essential. **Cal Raleigh** provides our best power-to-matchup ratio, capitalizing on a 4.87 xERA target to mitigate his modest park adjustment.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved the outfield slots, specifically the razor-thin margin between **Bryce Harper** (59.70) and **Justin Crawford** (49.66). Despite the need for speed\u2014where **Justin Crawford** is a natural asset\u2014his #9 lineup position effectively cannibalized his utility score, making him a marginal play. Conversely, **Bryce Harper**\u2019s elite 0.380 xwOBA and top-third batting order solidified his spot despite a challenging matchup against Jax. The bottom of our rotation, including **Gavin Sheets** and **JJ Bleday**, remains in the marginal bucket; they are active, but we are essentially streaming them to preserve our game caps while monitoring for any late-breaking lineup shifts.\n\nWe enter this slate without the services of **Daulton Varsho** and **Matt Chapman**, both of whom are sidelined on the IL, while **Tyler Freeman** remains buried in the minors. The absence of these contributors places a heavier burden on **Jonathan Aranda**, who is a sneaky strong play today at 64.34, bolstered by a 12% platoon advantage against Nola. We are proceeding with caution regarding the wind and any potential weather delays in the late-afternoon windows, but the lineup is optimized to maximize efficiency across our primary categories. As always, keep a close watch on **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Masyn Winn**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Braden Montgomery**\u2014should any of their respective clubs alter their deployment, we have depth ready to pivot to ensure our 5x5 targets remain within reach.",
